<title>UK: Prism Rail wins two UK rail franchises.</title>
<headline>Prism Rail wins two UK rail franchises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prism Rail Plc said it has won a 7-1/2 year franchise to operate rail services in South Wales and the west of England via the purchase of South Wales &amp; West Railway Ltd and Cardiff Railway Company Ltd.</p>
<p>Prism, set up to pursue opportunities from Britain's rail privatisation, said it will start operating the services from October 13.</p>
<p>The company already has one of the 25 British train companies currently being privatised - the LTS Rail suburban London franchise which it was awarded on May 9.</p>
</text>
